# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-compiled / cache
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.nbi
*.nbc
.numba_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / packaging artefacts
#
# dist/ holds the release archives built by pack_repo.ps1. They are
# deliverables, not sources: upload them as GitHub Release assets or a Zenodo
# deposit rather than committing them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulation data.
#
# Raw campaign output is ~2.5 GB and fully regenerable from run_campaign.py
# given the seeds recorded in each cell's `spec`, so legacy campaigns remain ignored. The three corrected
# rev20261026 campaigns are explicitly versioned with this manuscript. The small derived
# analysis tables in data/analysis/ ARE tracked: they are what the manuscript
# numbers come from and they are cheap to carry.
#
# Only the three explicitly listed corrected campaigns are versioned below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/*
!data/raw/rev20261026_shared/
!data/raw/rev20261026_powerlaw/
!data/raw/rev20261026_fgn/

# Standalone generator-calibration / validation arrays at the top level of
# data/ are regenerable and not needed to reproduce the manuscript numbers.
/data/*.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party literature.
#
# .lit/ contains published journal PDFs downloaded for reference and the text
# extracted from them. It is NOT distributed with this repository: those PDFs
# remain under the publishers' copyright, so redistributing them in a public
# repository is not appropriate. Every reference is listed in manuscript/refs.bib
# with its DOI, so the sources are citable and discoverable without shipping
# copies. Delete this rule if and only if you intend the deposit to remain
# private.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.lit/

# 600 dpi TIFF copies of the manuscript figures are submission assets, not
# sources: the repository carries PDF, SVG and PNG. Ignored TIFF files must
# be distributed separately; release packaging selects tracked files only.
figs/**/*.tiff

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local run artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.figpreview/
.dsh_tmp/
.planning/
manuscript/tmp/
.dsh_acl_recovery/
acl-report-*.jsonl
acl-backup-*.json
acl-backup-*.ps1

